==Battleground==
*The enemy base is protected by a [[Base Barrier]] until the boss is defeated.
*Infinite [[Doge Dark]]s spawn after 6.67 seconds<sup>200f</sup>, delay 16.67~20 seconds<sup>500f~600f</sup>.
*1 [[Suidae Piggicus]] spawns after 20 seconds<sup>600f</sup>.
*1 [[Xenobeast Bunaglios]] spawns as the boss after 33.33 seconds<sup>1,000f</sup>.
*5 [[Aku Doge]]s spawn after 40 seconds<sup>1,200f</sup>, delay 110~113.33 seconds<sup>3,300f~3,400f</sup>.
*1 [[Midnite D.]] spawns after 106.67 seconds<sup>3,200f</sup>.
*1 [[Suidae Piggicus]] spawns after 180 seconds<sup>5,400f</sup>.
*Infinite [[Suidae Piggicus|Suidae Piggici]] spawn after 340 seconds<sup>10,200f</sup>, delay 133.33 seconds<sup>4,000f</sup>.
*Infinite [[Midnite D.|Midnite Ds]] spawn after 420 seconds<sup>12,600f</sup>, delay 200 seconds<sup>6,000f</sup>.

==Strategy==
The difficulty takes a noticable spike here, making an already difficult stage even more deadly. The boss spawns on a timer, but does not give you a lot of time to prepare. Since a [[Base Barrier]] renders the enemy base indestructible until Xenobeast Bunaglios is defeated, any rush strategies are also out of the question. A [[Talents|Talented]] [[Hip Hop Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Can Can Cat]] will help immensely for the startup, as it can kill the Doge Darks for double the money, which helps tremendously in preparing for the boss.

Once the boss spawns, there are two primary strategies to defeat it, both equally viable and challenging:

Method 1:
By using an Attack Up (Sm) [[Cat Combo]], you can eliminate Bunaglios and Piggicus before Midnite D. appears. This strategy involves using high DPS, anti-Behemoth/Alien units—such as [[Elder Beast Naala (Special Cat)|Awakened Naala]], [[Miter Saw Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Neo Saw Cat]], and [[Master Uril (Special Cat)|Esoteric Uril]]—to deal heavy damage, while stalling and [[weaken]]ing the boss with [[Ancient Egg: N108 (Super Rare Cat)|Soap Cat]]. The key is to lure Bunaglios to the Cat Base and continuously chip away at its health with precise timing. Keep in mind that Bunaglios' [[Critical Hit]] RNG can sometimes be fatal, so while this method relies on brute forcing your way through, it tends to be less consistent than the alternative. Failing to kill Bunaglios off before Midnite D. assaults your front lines does not mean you have lost. By that point, your Esoteric Uril and [[Elder Mask Doron (Special Cat)|Awakened Doron]] should almost be off cooldown, so as long as you have reduced Bunaglios to at least 25% HP, you can still finish him off without much issue.

Method 2:
Alternatively, you can stall Bunaglios and Piggicus near the Enemy Base to conserve funds and prepare for Midnite D. This is typically the trickiest part, as the Doge Darks have 60,000 HP each, and will continuously kill your Soap Cats and [[Ancient Egg: N112 (Rare Cat)|Cat Egg Pods]]. Talented [[Cats in a Box (Special Cat)|Heavy Assault C.A.T.]] is recommended if you are struggling with defeating them. When Midnite D. eventually spawns, you can finish him off quickly rendering him a non-issue. To execute this strategy, first lure Midnite D. to the Cat Base. Then perform a precisely timed [[Bahamut Cat (Special Cat)|Awakened Bahamut Cat]] chain as follows:

#Allow Midnite D. to hit the Cat Base.
#Spawn [[Ancient Egg: N004 (Special Cat)|Supercar Cat]].
#Deploy [[Express Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Bullet Train Cat]] to break his shield.
#Call forth Awakened Bahamut Cat.
#Finally, spawn a well timed [[Slime Cat (Rare Cat)|Jelly Dumpling Cat]].

If executed correctly, these steps leave Midnite D. with a low enough health pool to be finished off by either Awakened Naala or Esoteric Uril. It's also recommended to equip a high level Slow Beam to prevent Bunaglios from catching up during this process. Once Midnite D. is dead, the clean up phase is not very difficult.

